[TITLE]
GUI annotation sections the solver never reads.

Legacy SWMM has no `case` for [LABELS], [BACKDROP] or [PROFILES] in parseLine,
so no engine parses or validates their content — which is why they are kept
verbatim rather than modelled. They used to be registered as no-op handlers, so
a model's labels and backdrop image were deleted by the first Open then Save.

Every value below is chosen to break a writer that tries to reformat instead of
replay: quoted strings with embedded spaces, a quoted name padded INSIDE the
quotes, an empty quoted field, a negative coordinate, and tab separators.

Note the section is [PROFILES], not [PROFILE]. Legacy matches section headers by
prefix so both are the same section there; this engine matches the whole tag,
and only "PROFILE" was registered — a spelling no deck in the corpus uses.

[OPTIONS]
FLOW_UNITS           CFS
FLOW_ROUTING         DYNWAVE
START_DATE           01/01/2024
END_DATE             01/02/2024
REPORT_STEP          00:15:00
ROUTING_STEP         00:00:30

[JUNCTIONS]
;;Name  Elev   MaxDepth
J1      100.0  10.0
J2       98.0  10.0

[OUTFALLS]
O1       90.0 FREE         NO

[CONDUITS]
;;Name  From  To  Length  Rough  InOff  OutOff
C1      J1    J2  100.0   0.013  0      0
C2      J2    O1  100.0   0.013  0      0

[XSECTIONS]
C1  CIRCULAR  1.5  0  0  0  1
C2  CIRCULAR  1.5  0  0  0  1

[COORDINATES]
J1  0    0
J2  100  0
O1  200  0

[LABELS]
;;X-Coord          Y-Coord            Label
119043.100         44310.420          "Outfall structure" "" "Arial" 10 1 0
-512.250           -44.500            "Below datum" "" "Times New Roman" 8 0 1

[BACKDROP]
FILE      	"Site Post.jpg"
DIMENSIONS	-0.123	0.000	1423.123	1475.000

[PROFILES]
;;Name          	Links
"profileA        "	C1	C2
